    {
      "id": "qtm-m2-quartiles-iqr-c3",
      "heading": "Quartiles of grouped data: formula and worked problem",
      "explanation_md": "**Formula for grouped data (class intervals):** Qk = L + ((k × n/4 - F) / f) × h\n\n- **Qk** = the k-th quartile (k = 1, 2, 3)\n- **L** = lower boundary of the quartile class\n- **n** = total frequency\n- **F** = cumulative frequency before the quartile class\n- **f** = frequency of the quartile class\n- **h** = width of the class interval\n\n**Slide problem:** classes 1-5 (6), 6-10 (19), 11-15 (13), 16-20 (20), 21-25 (12), 26-30 (11), 31-35 (6), 36-40 (5); cumulative frequency 6, 25, 38, 58, 70, 81, 87, 92. Find Q1, Q2, Q3. Here n = 92 and h = 5.\n\n**Q1** (k = 1): k × n/4 = 23, which falls in class 6-10 (cumulative 25). L = 5.5, F = 6, f = 19. Q1 = 5.5 + ((23 - 6)/19) × 5 = **9.97**.\n\n**Q2** (k = 2): 46, which falls in class 16-20 (cumulative 58). L = 15.5, F = 38, f = 20. Q2 = 15.5 + ((46 - 38)/20) × 5 = **17.5**.\n\n**Q3** (k = 3): 69, which falls in class 21-25 (cumulative 70). L = 20.5, F = 58, f = 12. Q3 = 20.5 + ((69 - 58)/12) × 5 = **25.08**.\n\nSo IQR = 25.08 - 9.97 = **15.11**.",
      "example_ids": [
        "qtm-ex-grouped-quartiles"
      ],
      "key_terms": [],
      "exam_line": "Grouped quartile: Qk = L + ((k n/4 - F)/f) x h. Find the class where cumulative frequency first reaches k n/4.",
      "clarification": null,
      "check_questions": [
        {
