    {
      "id": "qtm-m2-quartiles-iqr-q-8692b99e",
      "type": "long",
      "stem": "Calculate Q1, Q2, Q3 and the IQR for the grouped data (class intervals 1-5 to 36-40 with frequencies 6, 19, 13, 20, 12, 11, 6, 5).",
      "options": [],
      "answer": "",
      "accept": [],
      "explanation": "",
      "model_answer_md": "**Setup.** Cumulative frequencies: 6, 25, 38, 58, 70, 81, 87, 92, so n = 92 and h = 5. Formula: Qk = L + ((k × n/4 - F)/f) × h.\n\n**Q1** (k = 1): 92/4 = 23. First cumulative frequency above 23 is 25, class 6-10. L = 5.5, F = 6, f = 19. Q1 = 5.5 + ((23 - 6)/19) × 5 = 5.5 + 4.47 = **9.97**.\n\n**Q2** (k = 2): 46, class 16-20 (cumulative 58). L = 15.5, F = 38, f = 20. Q2 = 15.5 + ((46 - 38)/20) × 5 = **17.5**.\n\n**Q3** (k = 3): 69, class 21-25 (cumulative 70). L = 20.5, F = 58, f = 12. Q3 = 20.5 + ((69 - 58)/12) × 5 = 20.5 + 4.58 = **25.08**.\n\n**IQR** = Q3 - Q1 = 25.08 - 9.97 = **15.11**.\n\n**Conclusion.** The middle half of the observations lies within a band of about 15.11.",
